% undefined.elpi as data for the debugger (by hand until elpi-tools/reflect).
pred positive i:int.
pred check i:list int.

debug.declared positive [debug.i].
debug.declared check [debug.i].
debug.clause (check []) true "undefined.elpi:7".
debug.clause (check [X|Xs]) (X > 0, positive X, check Xs) "undefined.elpi:8".

% bridges: the only native clause of each predicate (see debug.elpi, section 6)
positive A :- debug.bridge (positive A).
check A :- debug.bridge (check A).
